---
name: plan-hardening-step-bead
version: 1.0.0
description: One plan-hardening step run as a bead, a child of the phase root, created by the runner before the step is dispatched. Its id is the step's ATM task id (`task_id` in the vars). `blocked_by` names the previous step bead and, for a review step, every finding bead filed by the previous review of the plan, so `bd ready` lists the step only when the planner has ruled on them. The runner closes it with the step's status and counts as the reason. Render strictly, then `jq -c .` into the import JSONL.
format: json
required_variables:
  - id
  - root
  - phase
  - step
  - cycle
  - route_to
defaults:
  blocked_by: []
---
{% if step not in [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6] %}ERROR: step must be 1 to 6, got {{ step }}
{% endif %}{
  "id": {{ id | tojson }},
  "title": {{ ("phase-" ~ phase ~ ": plan hardening step " ~ step ~ " cycle " ~ cycle ~ " (" ~ route_to ~ ")") | tojson }},
  "issue_type": "task",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 1,
  "description": {{ ("Run `.claude/skills/plan-hardening/steps/step-" ~ step ~ ".md`, cycle " ~ cycle ~ ", routed to " ~ route_to ~ ".") | tojson }},
  "labels": {{ ["phase-" ~ phase, "stage:plan-hardening", "step:" ~ step] | tojson }},
  "dependencies": [
    {"issue_id": {{ id | tojson }}, "depends_on_id": {{ root | tojson }}, "type": "parent-child"}{% for b in blocked_by %},
    {"issue_id": {{ id | tojson }}, "depends_on_id": {{ b | tojson }}, "type": "blocks"}{% endfor %}
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "step": {{ step }},
    "cycle": {{ cycle }},
    "route_to": {{ route_to | tojson }}
  }
}
